oney you deposit. Rules, contract specifications, fees and tax treatment change: always check the current values with your broker, exchange, firm ","3":"THIS JOURNAL BELONGS TO NAME ACCOUNT / BROKER ACCOUNT SIZE AT START JOURNAL NO. STARTED FINISHED TRADE NUMBERS IN THIS JOURNAL, FROM – TO IF FOUND, PLEASE CONTACT “Plan the trade, trade the plan, then write down what really happened.”","4":"HOW TO USE THIS JOURNAL TRADING JOURNAL ONCE, BEFORE YOU START (PAGES 6–10) Write your trading plan, read the mistake and emotion key (page 7), set your risk rules, describe your A, B and C game and number your setups. Thirty minutes, once. Every page after this one refers back to them. EVERY TRADE: THE BOLD BOXES FIRST Short on time? Fill the three boxes with a bold frame: Result R, Followed my rules and Mistake #. That takes twenty seconds and is enough for every statistic in this book. The rest of the card is for the trades worth studying. R, THE ONE NUMBER THAT MATTERS 1R is the money you planned to lose: the distance from entry to your initial stop, times your size. Result R = net P&L ÷ 1R. +2R means you made twice what you risked; −1R means the stop was hit as planned. R makes a $50 trade and a $5,000 trade comparable. R : R is always written risk : reward, e.g. 1 : 2. MAE / MFE: t","5":"EXAMPLE · A COMPLETED PAGE TRADE RECORDS MAR 9 TRADING JOURNAL WEEK OF NO. 201 TRADE STOCKS · OPTIONS · FUTURES · FOREX · CRYPTO DATE ASSET S O F FX C ACCOUNT INSTRUMENT OPTION strike · C/P · expiry SIDE SETUP TIMEFRAME 03/10 O Broker A AAPL 175 C · Apr 17 x Long Short Earnings drift daily ENTRY STOP TARGET 1 TARGET 2 SIZE units $ PER PT · PIP · TICK RISK $ RISK % CCY 3.20 1.60 6.40 2 ct $200 / pt 320 0.3% USD EXIT POINTS / PIPS GROSS COSTS fees · swap · funding NET RESULT R MAE · MFE R TIME IN TRADE 5.10 +1.90 +380 -1.30 +378.70 +1.18 -0.4 / +1.6 6 days SETUP GRADE EXECUTION GRADE FOLLOWED MY RULES ON MISTAKE # EMOTION CODE WOULD I TAKE IT AGAIN? A x B C x A B C x Entry x Management x Exit